\description{
\strong{Prefer this to \code{nrow(digest$fragments)} whenever the ion series matter, which for ETD is
always.} A bare total folds in the one extra full-length \code{z-dot} per peptide, which is not a
backbone-cleavage ion between two residues.
}
\details{
The \code{zDot} series runs \code{1..length}, not \code{1..length-1}. The extra ion numbered \code{length} is the
whole peptide minus NH2 - the N-Ca cleavage at residue 1 - which is \strong{correct and
deliberate}, not a defect. It is absent when the peptide starts with proline.

Note also that \code{zDot} counts come in \strong{below} \code{length} per peptide rather than above it,
because z-dot ions are suppressed N-terminal to proline while the complementary \code{c} ions are
not. On albumin that is 138 proline sites, 138 suppressed \code{z-dot} and \strong{0} suppressed \code{c}
(smith-chem-wisc/mzLib#1110).
}
\value{
A data.frame of \code{product_type} and \code{n}, ordered by product type.
}
